Turnip Darwin: a mapped reserve for command-stream BOs (the render server's), and counters.

SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
Copyright (c) 2026 Leo Zhang

tu_cs_add_bo maps every BO it adds; the BO cache gives back what it cached, mapped, so the CPU maps of WindowServer's encode
thread are new BOs: command buffers made anew after the runtime's command pools were trimmed or made, while every reclaim and the
2 s age empty the cache. Freed command-stream BOs (tu_cs_add_bo's flags: read only, dumpable) go to a reserve that keeps them
whole and mapped (no age, no reclaim flush, a byte budget: 32 MiB in WindowServer, TU_DARWIN_CS_RESERVE_MB elsewhere, LRU past
it), taken first by the next command stream of a fitting size (at most four times it), then a mapped cached BO, then any.
/private/var/ngpu/debug/no-cs-reserve (read once a second) switches it off at run time: the old path exactly. Counters every
10 s in the unified log (WindowServer, or TU_DARWIN_BO_REPORT=1): "NativeAdreno BO report: cs ... maps ...".
Against 0001-0013 (0013: gpu/bo-race1 546d848a, the BO struct cleared under the retire lock: the installed line's).

